  <Class>EC.02.06.01</Class>
  <Text>
      The consultants noted numerous areas in the hospital that had horizontal dust.  Examples include
      vending machines, offices and furniture and patient rooms.  Corners in rest rooms were unclean
      and paper towel dispensers were packed so tightly towels could be removed only in pieces
      which were thrown on the floor or were empty.  Base boards and bumper guards, particularly on
      the ground floor were dirty.
    </Text>
